# Frontend responsiveness

`AGENTS.md` is the source of truth. Apply on every `apps/web` change.

## Required

* Mobile- and iPad-friendly by default — not desktop-only with a later pass.
* Check layouts at phone (~375px), iPad portrait (~768px), and desktop.
* Responsive spacing/typography/stacking via MUI breakpoints (`xs` / `sm` / `md`).
* No horizontal overflow: wrap long filenames, emails, IDs, and URLs.
* Reachable primary actions on touch screens; account for top bar, bottom tabs, and safe areas (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`, `100dvh`).
* Compact nav on small viewports; permanent sidebar only from `md` up.

## Do not

* Ship fixed-width desktop rows that clip on phones.
* Rely on hover-only controls for critical actions.
* Ignore bottom/top chrome overlapping content on mobile.
